# host-text-joins-in-nfc: pins that text from the Host arrives as NFC and
# that joining two Host texts normalises the seam (chapter 3, Text; ADR
# 0030). The Request's second argument is a lone U+0301, which is already
# NFC and one Character, so it is written literally. Joined after "e", it
# composes to U+00E9, one Character, which is the Request's result. Fuel,
# allocation and state figures are estimates.
# Unblessed: the output lines are written by hand, not by bless.

> load joiner
> request d1 to=joiner message=join args=["e", "́"]
> pump clock=2026-09-30T09:00:00Z
seg joiner/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=join clause=1 fuel=38 alloc=24 state=24 end=return
run joiner/r1 outcome=completed delivery=d1 handler=join value="é" fuel=38 alloc=24
pumped state=idle fuel=38

> vars
vars joiner markLength=1 joinedLength=1
